{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22032 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Jatamanin C is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Jatamanin C directly targets SNU-387, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including Dendocarbin K and a related metabolite. These targets ultimately converge on Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, indicating a potential role for Jatamanin C in modulating this kinase activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Jatamanin C influences downstream signaling through the mitogen-activated protein kinase (MAPK) pathway, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a broad, interconnected network of targets, underscoring the complexity of the biological processes involved.",
